acter one two three storm  according to creative executive sydney  iwanter it was important to focus on  these characters real emotional  weaknesses well here's the thing they  just weren't typical superhero  vulnerabilities we're talking about  rogue not being able to touch anyone  without consequences absolutely storm  dealing with being orphaned and even  wolverine dealing with unrequited love  oh let's talk about the love triangle oh  my cyclops wolverine and jean grey and  poor wolverine he was supposed to be at  the wedding but he is mad because he is  in love with his frenemies wife jean  grey we all love jean grey i felt like  jean grey was like the glue would always  come in and kind of just make sure she  was the referee for everybody i can  sense his feelings  they seem genuine just like wolverine  that we see right here i used to put  forks between my fingers yes yes i  thought i was the only one i had my  mama's butter knife yeah i was walking  around the house thinking i was wobbling  boy if you don't put my butter knife  back in that drawer i just need pictures  of you in all your makeshift x-men  costumes and we can't forget about my  boy morph he was only supposed to be in  one episode but fox had a focus group  with a couple hundred kids and they  voted for morph as their favorite mutant  resurrected by popular demand the first  season had one continuous storyline but  due to animation delays season two's  episodes were created to stand on their  own so if one episode wasn't finished on  time another could be shown in its place  networks at the time didn't think kids  could follow complicated storylines the  series writing team disagreed which was  definitely the right call and on behalf  of kids everywhere we thank you director  larry houston who was also the very  first black saturday morning storyboard  artist to be hired in hollywood was a  big fan of legendary comic book artist  jim lee lee's x-men costume designs  varied between characters but shared  similar colors and overall style and  therefore inspired the look for the show  we love to see it and speaking of making  some changes in hollywood houston and  show runner eric leewall had a whole new  approach to casting the series the first  batch of audition tapes they received  were all too cartoonish voice actors at  the time weren't used to playing it  straight especially for a saturday  morning cartoon so they ended up  bringing in serious theater actors from  toronto to voice their x-men and these  actors brought a gravitas and a  grounding and a realness to each  character it was just so amazing to hear  it according to george busa who voiced  beast the cast had to record all their  dialogue lines first because their  voices would be so worn out after doing  battle noises like this marcellus oh  [Laughter]  still all that vocal strain paid off  before this cartoon came out we didn't  know how these characters sounded we did  not they were only on paper so this is  the first time for us as fans of the  comic books to actually hear the voice  of our favorite characters and we loved  it the series packed so much story into  22 minutes way more than other animated  shows at the time with 40 page scripts  consisting of 400 to 500 shots it took  more than 30 000 animated frames to make  a single episode totally unheard of for  a kid's cartoon this was way before a  computer animation so every single one  of those frames was painted by hand oh  my hands are crapping up just thinking  about all that painting and what about  the cameos from the other marvel heroes  we got captain america right here it was  already a big deal hello headline news  we got x-men and then you turned around  and we got new people ken i was just  starstruck we have to shout out eric  leewald and julia leewald we found their  book x-men the art and making of the  animated series super helpful when  making this episode if you're a fan of  the series you'll love that book make  sure you check it out and that's our  show for today be sure to like subscribe  and check out x-men the animated series  now streaming on disney bluff take care  of yourselves and the planet and we'll  see you next time marcellus and ken  signing off storm would be both of our  favorite characters that's because we  spend too much time together you love it  i do i do

